  "comments": [],
  "caption": "We’re chatting with creatives on the sights, sounds and feels of home (or wherever you make your bed). Swipe to see postcards from South Carolina-based photographer @stefannagram \n\nWHAT’S THE DRUMBEAT OF YOUR HOME?\n\nwarm, chaotic, safe, cozy, eccentric and lived-in\n\nTELL US ABOUT YOUR CREATIVE PROCESS\n\nI don’t have a distinct process, but I would say that when I have an idea or work with someone who has a specific vision and tone, I sit, think, and pray about how to bring it to life. I’ll scan Pinterest and magazines, lie down in bed or go outside to meditate and dream, go for a drive, consult with my husband and creative friends, pour myself some coffee or wine (or both), and maybe take a shower. \n\nWHAT DOES YOUR HOME FEEL LIKE?\n\nCozy cuddles in the living room, coffee on the back porch, baby giggles and fingerprints everywhere, meals around the table, friends and family gathered and lots and lots of cutie chaos.\n\nHOW DO YOU BALANCE BETWEEN YOUR WORK PROFESSIONALLY AND PERSONALLY?\n\nI think, for me, the balance comes from remembering that my life itself is worthy of being documented too. In a funny way, motherhood has brought me back to why I fell in love with photography in the first place: noticing and preserving the beauty of an ordinary life.\n\nHOW DOES YOUR SPACE HELP YOU STAY CREATIVE?\n\nI spend a lot of time at home... inside, outside, and all around, and because of that, I’ve really worked toward making my house cozy and unique so that every corner inspires me. I do a lot of thrifting/antiquing and I’m always moving things around or purging to keep things interesting and inspiring.",
